### Kevalon ERP — Module 16: User Management
### Base URL: http://localhost:5000/api/user
### Use VS Code REST Client extension to run these requests

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api/user
@adminToken = REPLACE_WITH_ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN
@companyId = REPLACE_WITH_COMPANY_ID
@secondCompanyId = REPLACE_WITH_SECOND_COMPANY_ID

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SCENARIO A: Invite a brand-new user to companyA
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1. Invite New User (creates user with null password + sends invite email)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": "{{companyId}}",
  "name": "Alice Sharma",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "phone": "+91-9876543210",
  "role": "Accountant"
}

### 2. Invite same email to companyA again (expect 409 — already has access)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": "{{companyId}}",
  "name": "Alice Sharma",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "role": "Manager"
}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SCENARIO B: Invite the same existing user to a second company
# (No new account — adds a companyAccess entry, returns 200)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 3. Grant Alice access to secondCompany (expect 200, not 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": "{{secondCompanyId}}",
  "name": "Alice Sharma",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "role": "CA"
}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SCENARIO C: List users for a company
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 4. List all active users for companyA
GET {{baseUrl}}?companyId={{companyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 5. List with search filter
GET {{baseUrl}}?companyId={{companyId}}&search=alice
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 6. Paginated listing
GET {{baseUrl}}?companyId={{companyId}}&page=1&limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 7. Include inactive users
GET {{baseUrl}}?companyId={{companyId}}&includeInactive=true
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SCENARIO D: Update role and profile
# Replace :userId with Alice's actual _id from step 1
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@userId = REPLACE_WITH_ALICE_USER_ID

### 8. Update Alice's role in companyA only
PUT {{baseUrl}}/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": "{{companyId}}",
  "role": "Manager"
}

### 9. Update Alice's global profile name (shared across companies)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": "{{companyId}}",
  "name": "Alice Sharma-Updated",
  "phone": "+91-9999999999"
}

### 10. Deactivate Alice in companyA only
PUT {{baseUrl}}/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": "{{companyId}}",
  "isActive": false
}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SCENARIO E: Revoke company access
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 11. Revoke access (soft revoke — isActive: false, user account preserved)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{userId}}?companyId={{companyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SCENARIO F: Self-lockout guard
# (caller tries to deactivate their own only active company)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@selfToken = REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_OWN_ACCESS_TOKEN
@selfId = REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_OWN_USER_ID

### 12. Self-lockout guard — PUT (expect 400)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/{{selfId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{selfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": "{{companyId}}",
  "isActive": false
}

### 13. Self-lockout guard — DELETE (expect 400)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{selfId}}?companyId={{companyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{selfToken}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SCENARIO G: Permission gate — Employee attempting to invite
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@employeeToken = REPLACE_WITH_EMPLOYEE_ACCESS_TOKEN

### 14. Employee attempts to invite user (expect 403 — insufficient permission)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": "{{companyId}}",
  "name": "Should Fail",
  "email": "fail@example.com",
  "role": "Sales"
}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SCENARIO H: Login attempt for invited-but-not-activated user
# Use POST /api/auth/login (not this module's endpoints)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 15. Login with invited email before setting password (expect 401 + clear message)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "any-password"
}
